---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Studio scheduling: kilns, wheels and classes"
	description="Kiln firing queues, class bookings and wheel and table reservations for pottery studios, run from one place instead of three clipboards."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Studio scheduling</p>
				<h1>Kilns, wheels and classes in one place.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					The kiln log is on a clipboard, wheel bookings are on the whiteboard and the class roster is
					in your inbox. Kilnbook keeps firings, wheel time and classes in one system, so you are not
					stitching the week together by hand.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="A studio floor with six wheels, a kiln room, drying shelves and a glaze table"
				width="480"
				height="309"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>One schedule for the whole studio</h2>
		<p>
			A Tuesday night class, a cone 6 glaze load and four members booked on the wheels all happen in
			the same building. In Kilnbook they live in the same place too, so the front desk answers "is
			my bowl out yet?" and "is a wheel free at 7?" from one system instead of three.
		</p>

		<h2>Kilns: what is loading and what is firing</h2>
		<p>
			Each kiln has its own queue for bisque, cone 6 and cone 10 glaze firings. You can see how full
			each load is, and Kilnbook keeps a firing log for every kiln with the date, cone and who loaded
			it. <a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes: courses, drop-ins and waitlists</h2>
		<p>
			Six-week courses, Saturday drop-ins and class packs sit alongside everything else. When a class
			is full, students join the waitlist, and a cancelled seat is offered to the next person by
			text. <a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Wheels and tables: booked by the hour</h2>
		<p>
			Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and shared equipment like the slab roller in
			one-hour blocks, with limits you set per membership tier. Freed-up slots appear on the calendar
			right away. <a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Base>
